.TH RUFUS 1 2026-10-27 "Rufus 4.16" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rufus \- create bootable USB drives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rufus
.RB [ \-x ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR FILESYSTEM ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR LOCALE ]
.RB [ \-i ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rufus
formats USB drives and makes them bootable, from Windows and Linux ISO images,
disk images (raw, compressed, VHD or VHDX), FreeDOS or a boot loader of its own.
It can also check the drive for bad blocks, compute the hashes of an image,
download Windows ISOs and save a drive or an optical disc to an image.
.PP
This is an unofficial port of Rufus to Linux, with a Qt 6 user interface. It
runs as the user: the writes go through
.BR rufus\-helper ,
which
.BR pkexec (1)
starts as root, with a single prompt for the session (the polkit action
.BR ie.rufus.helper ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-iso =\fIPATH\fR
Select the image at
.I PATH
when Rufus starts. A
.I PATH
without
.B \-i
does the same.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filesystem =\fIFILESYSTEM\fR
Prefer this file system when formatting: FAT, FAT32, NTFS, UDF, exFAT, ext2,
ext3 or ext4 (or the number of one of them).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-locale =\fILOCALE\fR
Use the language of
.I LOCALE
(such as
.BR pl\-PL ),
rather than the one of the desktop.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extra\-devs
List USB hard drives too (Alt\-F in the window).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Copy the log to the standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rufus/rufus.ini
The settings.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Rufus
The files that Rufus downloads: boot loaders, revocation lists, ISOs.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUFUS_HELPER
The path of the helper, instead of the one of the installation.
.TP
.B RUFUS_LOC
A localization file to use instead of the one of the installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rufus\-cli (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
https://github.com/mikigal/rufus\-linux
